      "side": 1,
      "message": "You make a good point. I think either would be difficult to understand :\n・The way to construct the diff to tell to netd is unobvious, so I don\u0027t think we should have this var called rangesToTellNetdToAdd and construct it the way the code does.\n・But you make a good point that removing the currently blocked UIDs mean that what we need to add is what this variable ends up storing.\n\nWith this in mind, I fixed the semantics :\n・Kept the current var and the current building style, but leave the ranges that should be blocked inside.\n・Introduced a new local called rangesToTellNetdToAdd that is now built from rangesThatShouldBeBlocked.\n\nI think this should clear the ambiguity. What do you think ?",
